      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T01:05:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this not simply what happens if you request both LOW_LATENCY and HIGH_BANDWIDTH as separate capabilities? AIUI there\u0027s no rule limiting a network request to a single capability. If these capabilities don\u0027t work together, then I think we have a bigger problem.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "2ef2366e331ace5bb1815a3d0c4ef5d9622baf0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "48e8acf2_586007e5",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T04:54:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "initial idea was to make it look like a standalone capability. Problem with allowing this to be added capability is that users can request with ENTERPRISE+HIGH_BANDWIDTH. But we can always document and add check for the same. I will check internally on how the semantics should be taken forward and based upon that decide whether to stick with current one or not",
      "parentUuid": "f6b608a6_0bdcde08",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "2ef2366e331ace5bb1815a3d0c4ef5d9622baf0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
