    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a84f621_dca89dda",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 600,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T01:07:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is \"HIGH\" in this case? URLLC has a semantic meaning in 5G, so a Slice that has type URLLC can be mapped, but I\u0027m not aware of a semantic meaning for \"HIGH_BANDWIDTH\". ISTM that we need to clearly define it either concretely or in terms of other standards. Otherwise, who is to say that an APN is high-bandwidth or not?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 600,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 600,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "2ef2366e331ace5bb1815a3d0c4ef5d9622baf0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61aa7a60_cfabaa20",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 600,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T04:54:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "again, these dont have direct mapping with standards. It need not even mean that slice. It\u0027s behavior can change based upon which network is processing it.",
      "parentUuid": "1a84f621_dca89dda",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 600,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 600,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "2ef2366e331ace5bb1815a3d0c4ef5d9622baf0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb121bfa_9ec94f82",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 600,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T17:37:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These definitely don\u0027t need to map to a pre-existing standard, but if they don\u0027t, then we have to be able to provide a clear contract between users and implementers so that a user knows what they are asking for when they put HIGH_BANDWIDTH and the platform knows what it has to provide to fulfill HIGH_BANDWIDTH. Otherwise, we don\u0027t have much of an API contract.\n\nFor ULL you can add a comment and just say that the network provides a latency characteristic at least as good as or better than the 5QI of a URLLC connection, which would be an easy way to make the contract clear... but it\u0027s also fine to use something different, as long as both user and platform can reliably agree on a meaning. It also has to mean the same thing over time, which adds to the challenge since HIGH_BANDWIDTH a decade ago was not HIGH_BANDWIDTH today.",
      "parentUuid": "61aa7a60_cfabaa20",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 600,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 600,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "2ef2366e331ace5bb1815a3d0c4ef5d9622baf0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2e9bbc9_3e3d082e",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 600,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T23:13:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is intentional to specify quantify how much of an improvement these network slices will give. Also this can have different meaning based upon transport.",
      "parentUuid": "cb121bfa_9ec94f82",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 600,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 600,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "2ef2366e331ace5bb1815a3d0c4ef5d9622baf0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1d35a16_1824b3b0",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 600,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T23:53:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One other thought. NetworkCapabilities.Builder() already has a method to setLinkDownstreamBandwidthKbps() and setLinkUpstreamBandwidthKbps(), so if the request is transport-specific and not some kind of fixed/minimum guaranteed universal value, that\u0027s probably a better API shape, even if you have to add things closer to setSubcribedDownstreamBandwidth() or something, which would allow a value in kbps. Otherwise, a universal capablity with transport-specific and otherwise undefined meaning seems problematic.",
      "parentUuid": "a2e9bbc9_3e3d082e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 600,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 600,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "2ef2366e331ace5bb1815a3d0c4ef5d9622baf0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2282cd46_c6ae3601",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 600,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-20T02:32:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are not trying to set a specific bandwidth for a transport, we are trying to get better bandwidth or lower latency than the default network. How much that is going to be will vary based upon the network, transport",
      "parentUuid": "d1d35a16_1824b3b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 600,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 600,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "2ef2366e331ace5bb1815a3d0c4ef5d9622baf0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8bf8609_3d82b45f",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 600,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-20T02:36:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, so that\u0027s something... a network with NET_CAPABILITY_HIGH_BANDWIDTH cannot be the default network. That\u0027s a constraint. It also must offer higher bandwidth (measured \u003csomewhere\u003e) than the default on that same transport (if available)...\n\n@Jean, is that the case? A HIGH_BANDWIDTH network will not be allowed to become DEFAULT?",
      "parentUuid": "2282cd46_c6ae3601",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 600,
        "startChar": 28,
